  "slug": "doubling-genome-bb89",
  "summary": "Recent tools recover genetic variants jointly with methylation and chromatin features, from single assays to pangenome-based satellite and transposon analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is sequencing-based detection of genomic variation read against epigenetic or chromatin context. UMR-seq captures unmethylated regions and sequences genetic variants in one assay, enabling population-scale analysis across diverse plant species. GraffiTE v1.1 genotypes structural variants, annotates polymorphic transposable elements, and maps long-read methylation onto them. Yruler measures Y chromosome satellite array length, composition and dosage directly from reads using pangenome assemblies, without alignment. The Segmentome provides a segment-level methylome representation inferred by an unsupervised Bayesian HMM from WGBS data across 207 samples. The newer element is pairing variant detection with methylation or chromatin state within a single workflow. The items are heterogeneous, so this thread describes the dominant pattern rather than a feature shared by all four.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
